Subject: [#94-11-459] Pentium Bug

In case you haven't been reading comp.sys.intel;

There is a floating point math error in most Pentium chips out there
at present. The bug manifest itself in the fp division of certain numbers.

Intel claims that most users will not experience the defect and seems
to be taking the position that replacement CPU's are on a *need* only
basis.

There is an assembly language routine you can get to check your 
machine at:

math.ucdavis.edu

 /pub/fdiv

to get the Intel position or to bitch in general:
800-628-8686(916-356-3551 international)
FaxBack number=(503)264-6835

This produced the error in my spreadsheet and MathCad: 
x= 4195835.0   y=3145727.0 (you want floating point numbers here)

delta=[x-(x/y)*y]

delta of course should be zero.

ackthpppt! (the result I got was 256?!)

