I also went to Montessori schools until 3rd grade.  I view it as the most
important thing my parents ever did for me: they teach one to *love*
learning (though they might not have taught me to spell Montessori).

I can rant for hours about the differences between the Montessori
schools and "good" traditional schools (they claimed that the one I
was sent to later was good -- they had no choice, since there were
no others for kids older than 1-2nd grade in my area).

My most vivid memories are of the games they had us play to learn
mathematics (how's the "bank game" grab ya, Extropes?) and the informal
experimentation they had us do to answer questions.  It definitely
showed us that the learning process can be (should be) fun.

I recommend, in the strongest possible terms, sending one's children
to Montessori schools.
